## K0400 -- a kernel fn that calls a function (PTX/SPIR-V kernels take scalar arithmetic, let and if only).
## command: lume agent kernel   (this file shows the diagnostic: the gate runs a copy named .src; K0400_kernel_outside_fragment.fixed.src is the corrected program)
## fix: keep kernel bodies to scalar arithmetic, let and if
kernel fn bad_k(x: int) -> int / gpu = count("abc") + x
print bad_k(1)
